---
/**
 * The floor of the instrument: the same model measured four times against the same ladder, twice
 * with Stockfish limited by time and twice limited by nodes (A2 of the P6 plan).
 *
 * Every row is one full run of the Elo suite. The bar is the 95 % interval, the mark is the
 * estimate. Nothing differs between the two rows of a group but the seed, so the distance between
 * them is what the instrument itself adds to a measurement: an Elo difference smaller than that
 * floor is not a difference. The two groups are the two ways of capping Stockfish, and the spread
 * of each is the number that decided which cap the milestone keeps (`decision`).
 *
 * Data comes from `src/data/ladder-floor.json`, written by `labs/m6/ladder_floor_export.py` and
 * copied here with `pnpm sync:data`; the schema is in `src/data/README.md`. With the committed
 * placeholder (`meta.generated: null`, no runs) the figure renders its "pendiente" state, because
 * a floor invented for the drawing would be the opposite of what it is here to show.
 *
 * Styles live in `src/styles/global.css` (`.fig*`): a scoped `<style>` in a figure used from MDX
 * never reaches the page.
 */
import raw from '../../data/ladder-floor.json';
import { formatInt } from '../../lib/format';

type Limit = 'time' | 'nodes';

interface Run {
  name: string;
  limit: Limit;
  elo: number;
  lo: number;
  hi: number;
}

interface LadderFloor {
  meta: { generated: string | null; model?: string; games?: number };
  runs: Run[];
  decision?: Limit | null;
}

const data = raw as LadderFloor;
const runs = Array.isArray(data.runs)
  ? data.runs.filter((run) => run && typeof run.elo === 'number')
  : [];
const ready = data.meta?.generated !== null && runs.length > 0;

const LIMITS: { key: Limit; title: string; word: string }[] = [
  { key: 'time', title: 'Stockfish limitado por tiempo', word: 'tiempo' },
  { key: 'nodes', title: 'Stockfish limitado por nodos', word: 'nodos' },
];

const groups = LIMITS.map((limit) => {
  const own = runs.filter((run) => run.limit === limit.key);
  const spread =
    own.length >= 2
      ? Math.max(...own.map((run) => run.elo)) - Math.min(...own.map((run) => run.elo))
      : null;
  return { ...limit, runs: own, spread, chosen: data.decision === limit.key };
}).filter((group) => group.runs.length > 0);

/* Axis fitted to the data and rounded outwards to a multiple of 50, padded so no bar touches the
   edge; a fixed axis would squash four intervals that differ by a handful of points. */
const ends = runs.flatMap((run) => [run.lo, run.hi]);
const pad = ready ? Math.max((Math.max(...ends) - Math.min(...ends)) * 0.1, 10) : 0;
const LOW = ready ? Math.floor((Math.min(...ends) - pad) / 50) * 50 : 0;
const HIGH = ready ? Math.ceil((Math.max(...ends) + pad) / 50) * 50 : 1;
const step = HIGH - LOW > 400 ? 100 : 50;
const ticks: number[] = [];
for (let value = LOW; value <= HIGH; value += step) ticks.push(value);

const X0 = 150;
const X1 = 615;
const x = (elo: number) => X0 + ((elo - LOW) / (HIGH - LOW || 1)) * (X1 - X0);

/* Vertical layout: a title line per group, then one row per run. */
const ROW = 28;
const HEAD = 26;
const TOP = 14;
let cursor = TOP;
const laid = groups.map((group) => {
  const titleY = cursor + 12;
  cursor += HEAD;
  const rows = group.runs.map((run) => {
    const y = cursor + ROW / 2;
    cursor += ROW;
    return { run, y };
  });
  cursor += 10;
  return { ...group, titleY, rows };
});
const axisY = cursor + 6;
const HEIGHT = axisY + 26;

const spreadText = (spread: number | null) =>
  spread === null ? 'una sola tirada' : `${formatInt(spread)} Elo entre tiradas`;

const summary = laid
  .map(
    (group) =>
      `Por ${group.word}: ${group.runs
        .map(
          (row) =>
            `${row.name} en ${formatInt(row.elo)}, intervalo ${formatInt(row.lo)} a ${formatInt(row.hi)}`,
        )
        .join('; ')}. ${spreadText(group.spread)}.`,
  )
  .join(' ');
const decisionText = data.decision
  ? `Se decidió limitar por ${LIMITS.find((l) => l.key === data.decision)?.word ?? data.decision}.`
  : '';
---

{ready ? (
  <figure class="fig fig--ladder" data-ladder-floor data-state="ready">
    <svg
      viewBox={`0 0 640 ${HEIGHT}`}
      role="img"
      aria-label={`Cuatro mediciones del mismo modelo contra la misma escalera. ${summary} ${decisionText}`}
    >
      <g font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--muted)">
        {ticks.map((tick) => (
          <g>
            <line
              x1={x(tick)}
              y1={TOP - 4}
              x2={x(tick)}
              y2={axisY}
              stroke="var(--line-soft)"
              stroke-width="1"
            />
            <text x={x(tick)} y={axisY + 16} text-anchor="middle" font-size="9">
              {tick}
            </text>
          </g>
        ))}
        <line x1={X0} y1={axisY} x2={X1} y2={axisY} stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="0.8" />
        <text x="10" y={axisY + 16} font-size="9">
          Elo medido
        </text>

        {laid.map((group) => (
          <g
            class={
              group.chosen ? 'fig-ladder__group fig-ladder__group--chosen' : 'fig-ladder__group'
            }
          >
            <text x="10" y={group.titleY} fill="var(--ink)" font-size="10">
              {group.title}
              {group.chosen ? ' · elegido' : ''}
            </text>
            {group.rows.map(({ run, y }) => (
              <g>
                <text x="10" y={y + 4} font-size="10">
                  {run.name}
                </text>
                <rect
                  x={x(run.lo)}
                  y={y - 6}
                  width={Math.max(x(run.hi) - x(run.lo), 1)}
                  height="12"
                  rx="2"
                  fill={group.chosen ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--diagram-stroke)'}
                  fill-opacity="0.22"
                  stroke={group.chosen ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--line)'}
                  stroke-width="0.8"
                />
                <line
                  x1={x(run.elo)}
                  y1={y - 8}
                  x2={x(run.elo)}
                  y2={y + 8}
                  stroke={group.chosen ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--ink)'}
                  stroke-width="1.6"
                />
                <text x={x(run.hi) + 6} y={y + 4} font-size="9" fill="var(--ink)">
                  {formatInt(run.elo)}
                </text>
              </g>
            ))}
          </g>
        ))}
      </g>
    </svg>
    <dl class="fig-ladder__spreads">
      {laid.map((group) => (
        <div class="fig-ladder__spread">
          <dt class="label">Por {group.word}</dt>
          <dd>
            {group.runs.map((run) => formatInt(run.elo)).join(' y ')}
            {' → '}
            <strong>{spreadText(group.spread)}</strong>
            {group.chosen ? ' · elegido' : ''}
          </dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
    <figcaption class="caption">
      Mismo modelo, misma escalera, mismas posiciones: solo cambia la semilla. La distancia entre
      las dos tiradas de cada grupo es lo que el instrumento añade por su cuenta, y por debajo de
      ella no hay diferencia que publicar.
      {data.meta.model ? ` Modelo: ${data.meta.model}.` : ''}
      {typeof data.meta.games === 'number'
        ? ` ${formatInt(data.meta.games)} partidas por tirada.`
        : ''}
      {decisionText ? ` ${decisionText}` : ''}
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
) : (
  <figure class="fig fig--pending" data-ladder-floor data-state="pending">
    <p class="fig__pending-main">
      <strong>Pendiente:</strong> el suelo del instrumento se dibuja con{' '}
      <code>src/data/ladder-floor.json</code>, que genera{' '}
      <code>labs/m6/ladder_floor_export.py</code> a partir de las cuatro tiradas reales y llega aquí
      con <code>pnpm sync:data</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="caption fig__pending-note">
      Lo que se mira es cuánto se mueve el Elo cuando no cambia nada más que la semilla. Un suelo
      inventado respondería a esa pregunta con una mentira, así que hasta que las tiradas terminen
      aquí no hay figura.
    </p>
  </figure>
)}
